      "writtenOn": "2023-10-02T23:11:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Neither the Android API guidelines nor Google best Java practices assert a particular direction on this type of pattern, so this comes down to stylistic preference AFAIK.\n\nPersonally, given the way this is represented in the current patchset matches the parameter pattern across the rest of the API with respect to how `needEncryption` is specified in the builder API for various fields, I think this is okay as is.\n\nClients who don\u0027t care about encryption can still use the simpler existing API which doesn\u0027t include the param, so we ensure backwards compatibility. \n\nThus, resolving this comment but please feel free to reopen if further discussion needed.",
      "parentUuid": "584ad81c_f8ad22c3",
